# SCRATCH.md is a log that every branch appends an entry to, so any two
# branches change the same place, the end of the file, and git calls that a
# conflict although the answer is always "keep both".  `merge=union` makes git
# give that answer by itself: where both sides changed the same lines it keeps
# both sides' lines and writes no conflict markers.
#
# Three things to know about it.
#
# It works for merges, rebases and cherry-picks made by a git that can see
# this file.  GitHub's merge button does not apply merge drivers from
# .gitattributes and still reports the conflict, so a branch may have to be
# merged or rebased locally before GitHub will take it.
#
# The blank line that both appended entries begin with comes out once, not
# twice, so the second entry's `## ` heading arrives with no blank line above
# it.  Put one back after the merge.
#
# And union never asks.  A line that both sides edited is kept in both
# versions, one after the other, with nothing to say so.  That is why TODO.md
# is deliberately NOT listed here although branches append to it too: it is
# also edited in place, a section's status in its heading, a task ticked off,
# and merged with union each of the nine branches it was tried against came
# out with one heading doubled.  There a visible conflict is the safer failure.
SCRATCH.md merge=union
